 "premises": ["P1 Block ids are bytes: every value 0..255 is treated as possible in the layout RAM (the loader's layout and runtime edits are not enumerated); the lookups also produce id $FF with surface 0 when the cell pointer leaves $C000-$CFFF. The bounds below hold for every id.", "P2 The header table is the ROM table at physical $38000 (bank 14, CPU $8000): D2E0 is stored once, by the loader (physical $2A71), from the first word of the record it reads, and that word is $8000 in all nine verified records (every act of zones 0-15 with act <= 2, including the five stages). Records outside those nine (R3 U3) are not covered: for them D2E0 is whatever the record holds.", "P3 D364, D353 and D36B are written only by the instructions listed in writer_census (byte search of the whole image). Register-addressed stores and block moves with an unresolved destination (DECOMP-1D R2 census; inherited U5) are not excluded as writers by this task.", "P4 An interrupt does not run the lookup routines or change the variables between a lookup and its jump (IM 1 reach: interrupt_reach); the interrupt handler's own transfers into slot-2 code are recorded, not followed (R3 premise P3 restores the mapper).", "P5 Entry into each dispatcher's code is by the paths listed in entry_6972, entry_77EC and entry_points. Byte-search hits that are not instruction starts of the known-code universe (reset/IM 1/NMI, per-frame code, every object type's callback closure) are classified; those outside it are not shown to be data (R2 policy), are reported, and the conclusions assume they are not executed.", "P6 Standard Sega mapper semantics (DECOMP-1D R4) and the R3 mapper premises for slot 1 (bank 1) and the slot-2 banks the callers set."],
